 "total_bytes": 3685904,
 "notes": [
  "Every npz carries meta_json (0-d str): json.loads(str(z['meta_json'])) documents each array and the checks.",
  "Paths (F1 path_flat, F-deg *_path_flat) are [k, 2] (query i, target j), 0-based, -1 = gap, FORWARD order.",
  "F2/F2b/F2c q: per-element fp16 ulp counts are misleading near 0 (F2 reference vs NERSC: max 9 element ulps, 6 elements > 1 ulp) while every difference is <= 0.5 ulp of the ROW's max |q| (q_diff_stats).",
  "margin_t = per residue min_k |h_t,k| (float64 re-evaluation). Bits with |h_t| < 1e-4: F2 3, F2b 1, F2c 1, Fdeg 0; an encoder with a different fp32 summation order may flip exactly those.",
  "F-deg expected values come from the float64 oracle WITH S5/S7. The research fp32 kernel (no S7) is wrong on degenerate rows/columns (affine-coefficient cancellation): e.g. case n1 kernel 0.5 vs oracle 0.776228; kept only as a diagnostic (real_q90_kernel_noS7).",
  "Real ESM3 distinct codes per item (length): allX30 28/30, His6 6/6, polyA50 38/50, Met1 1/1, GS 2/2, angiotensinI 10/10.",
  "F-tok: S15 upper-cases '<mask>' to '<MASK>', which ESM3 does not treat as special, so every normalised case is length-preserving; the multi-character collapse only happens on raw (un-normalised) input.",
  "F4: m = 32.58 and 594.92 lie just outside the table (centres 32.5844 / 594.9176). High-m rows carry both the research clamp and an UNCAPPED ln-m extrapolation; D15 decides.",
  "F2b rows are not stored: load tests/resources/embeddings/{1acb.A,2uzi.A}.pt with map_location='cpu'."
 ],
 "plan_tolerances": {
  "F1": "paths 50/50 identical; S_f/S_r rel <= 1e-5; Q90 abs <= 1e-3; lnE abs <= 1e-3 at N=1e9; 3 pairs survive E <= 1e-3",
  "F2": "code bits >= 0.99999; q within 1 fp16 ulp",
  "F2b/F2c": "codes identical to the reference encoder",
  "F3": "Q90 abs <= 1e-3",
  "F4": "rel <= 1e-12",
  "F-deg": "synthetic: abs <= 1e-5 vs reference with S7; no NaN; NaN q raises"
 },
